 **Min-Max Octree:**
 The octree is built directly around voxels (as opposed to cells) [S5, unofficial]. Each node in the octree stores aggregate information derived from its children:
-*   **Internal Nodes:** Store the minimum ($min$) and maximum ($max$) scalar values of all voxels in their subtree. These values are used to determine if the isosurface threshold $T$ lies within the node's range. If the threshold $T$ falls outside the stored $[min, max]$ range, the node is pruned [G].
